==Slovene==
{{wp|lang=sl}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|sl|ſtrah}} {{q|Bohorič alphabet}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sl|sla-pro|*straxъ}}, from {{inh|sl|ine-bsl-pro|*strākš-}}, from {{inh|sl|ine-pro|*(s)treg-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sl-IPA|strȃh}}
* {{rhymes|sl|aːx}}
* {{hyphenation|sl|strah}}

===Noun===
{{sl-noun|strȃh|m-in}}

# [[fear]]
#: {{syn|sl|bojazen|panika|plahota|pristrah|tesnoba}}
# {{lb|sl|archaic}} [[horror]], [[unpleasantness]]{{sl-ref|SSKJ}}
#: {{syn|sl|groza|grozota|srh|prepast}}
#: {{uxi|sl|'''Strah''' je, če zapade dva metra snega.|'''It''' is '''horrible''' if two meters of snow fall.}}
# [[phantom]], [[ghost]] {{gloss|a scary mythical creature}}
#: {{syn|sl|fantom|duhovina|strašilo|bavbav}}

====Usage notes====
To express that someone is scared, impersonal ''be'' is used:
* {{uxi|sl|Strah me je psov.|I am scared of dogs.|lit=There is fear of dogs to me.}}
See the usage notes under ''{{l|sl|biti}}'' for more information.

